  "findings": [
    "1.6.1 selects the `landmark_genes` list while loading (hyperparameter `gene_list`; a missing gene raises). The v2 `ElasticNet` preset uses `scaledGeneExpression`, which has no gene-list option and scales the whole view, so the preset trains on every gene of the dataset. Compared at the estimator-input level on a pre-selected matrix. To be fixed by packages A1/B5.",
    "v2 holds features as float32 end to end (`DenseViewFeaturizer` casts to float32, so the estimator receives a float32 matrix); 1.6.1 computes in float64. Features therefore agree to ~1e-7 relative (class forward), not exactly. Ridge solves in float32 in v2: refitting sklearn Ridge on the same matrix in float32 vs float64 differs by 2.4e-5 absolute (predictions ~7), which is the whole Ridge difference (class train).",
    "1.6.1 builds `sklearn.ElasticNet(alpha, l1_ratio)` with sklearn's solver defaults (max_iter=1000, tol=1e-4, cyclic); v2 pins max_iter=2000, tol=1e-2, selection='random', random_state=0. All are overridable in v2, and with the sklearn values the coefficients agree to 6e-8 (class forward). With the preset values they only agree statistically (deviation steps).",
    "The first 1.6.1 hyperparameter set (l1_ratio=0, alpha=1) is `Ridge`; v2 also maps l1_ratio=0 to `Ridge`, so both estimator types agree.",
    "v2 changed the default alpha to 0.1 (the 1.6.1 grid starts at 1); the case sets alpha explicitly on both sides."
  ],
